{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Behold.</b> Those who burn against you — from the nifal pattern, from the root חרי אף (Exodus 11:8), like נחרו בי (Song of Songs 1:6). The meaning concerns the children of Babylon, for at the time of visiting them and destroying them, He visited His children and they returned to their border by the command of Cyrus."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:20.297005281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}